questions.text:
What is the output of the following code?

class Animal:
    def sound(self):
        print('Generic animal sound')
class Dog(Animal):
    def sound(self):
        print('Woof')
dog = Dog()
dog.sound()

What happens when you call a method of a parent class that is overridden by the child class in the following code?

class Animal:
    def sound(self):
        print('Generic animal sound')

class Dog(Animal):
    def sound(self):
        print('Woof')

dog = Dog()
dog.sound()

What is the method resolution order (MRO) of the following classes?

class Animal:
    pass

class Mammal(Animal):
    pass

class Dog(Mammal):
    pass

Why does the following code raise an AttributeError?

class A:
    def __init__(self):
        self attr = 'A'

class B(A):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__() # Does not set self.attr

class C(B):
    def __init__(self):
        print(self.attr)

c = C()

Why can't you simply call a parent class's method using its class name in the following code?

class Animal:
    def sound(self):
        print('Generic animal sound')

class Dog(Animal):
    def sound(self):
        print('Woof')
dog = Dog()
dog.sound()

Why does the following code raise a TypeError when trying to sort a list of objects?

class Person:
    def __lt__(self, other):
        return self.age < other.age

people = [Person(age=20), Person(age=30), Person(age=10)]
people.sort()
